<section><h2 class="ref-sec-title">Events</h2><ol class="day-events yr-events"><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/february-7">7 February</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Great Baltimore Fire begins</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">A fire broke out in a dry-goods warehouse and burned for some 30 hours, destroying more than 1,500 buildings in central Baltimore. Fire crews from other cities could not connect hoses to local hydrants.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/russo-japanese-war" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/russo-japanese-war.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/february-8">8 February</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Japan attacks the Russian fleet at Port Arthur</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">Japanese <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/torpedo">torpedo</a> boats struck the Russian Pacific squadron at night, opening the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russo-japanese-war">Russo-Japanese War</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/japan">Japan</a>'s victory in 1905 was the first by an Asian power over a European one in modern times.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag tih-tag-profile" href="/empire/russian-empire">Russian Empire</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russo-japanese-war">Russo-Japanese War</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/april-8">8 April</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Britain and France sign the Entente Cordiale</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">A set of agreements settled colonial disputes, with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/britain">Britain</a> recognised in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/egypt">Egypt</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/morocco">Morocco</a>. The understanding ended centuries of rivalry and drew the two powers together before 1914.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/may-4">4 May</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">United States takes over the Panama Canal works</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The US formally took possession of the abandoned French canal project. Completed in 1914, the canal spared ships the long voyage around <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/south-america">South America</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/south-america">South America</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/october-20">20 October</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Chile and Bolivia sign the Treaty of Peace and Friendship</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">Signed in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/santiago">Santiago de Chile</a> twenty years after the end of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/war-of-the-pacific">War of the Pacific</a>, the treaty set the boundary between the two countries through 96 points from Cerro Zapaleri to Cerro Chipe. It also regulated relations between them.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag tih-tag-profile" href="/empire/republic-of-chile">Republic of Chile</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/war-of-the-pacific">War of the Pacific</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/october-27">27 October</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">The New York City Subway opens</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The Interborough Rapid Transit Company opened <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-york">New York</a>'s first underground line, from City Hall to 145th Street. Around 150,000 people rode on the first day of a network that grew into one of the world's largest.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-york">New York</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/theatre" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/theatre.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/december-27">27 December</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Peter Pan opens on the London stage</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">J. M. Barrie's play Peter Pan, or the Boy Who Wouldn't Grow Up opened at the Duke of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/york">York</a>'s <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/theatre">Theatre</a>. Its story of Neverland, Captain Hook and Tinker Bell became a children's classic.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/theatre">Theatre</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/london">London</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">Battle</p><h3 class="tih-event-title"><a href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-waterberg">Battle of Waterberg</a></h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The Battle of Waterberg was fought on 11 August 1904 at the Waterberg plateau in German South West Africa, now Namibia, between German troops under Lothar von Trotha and the Herero.</p></div></li></ol></section>
