<section><h2 class="ref-sec-title">In the profiles</h2><ul class="yr-prof"><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/congo-free-state"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Congo%20Free%20State.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Congo Free State</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Roger Casement’s report is published and the Congo Reform Association is founded</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/french-west-africa"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/French%20West%20Africa.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>French West Africa</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Ernest Roume’s decree gives the federation its own administration and budget in Dakar</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/culture/bell-beaker-culture"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Bell%20Beaker%20culture.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Bell Beaker culture</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">John Abercromby introduces the English name Bell Beaker</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/oriental-republic-of-uruguay"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Oriental%20Republic%20of%20Uruguay.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Oriental Republic of Uruguay</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The last Blanco rising ends at the Battle of Masoller with the death of Aparicio Saravia; President José Batlle y Ordóñez's reforms follow.</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/work/iliad"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Iliad.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Iliad</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Suleyman al-Boustani publishes his complete translation, the first of the Iliad into Arabic</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/battle/battle-of-tsushima"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Battle%20of%20Tsushima.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Battle of Tsushima</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Japanese destroyers attack the Russian Far East Fleet at Port Arthur and the Russo-Japanese War begins</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/battle/battle-of-tsushima"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Battle%20of%20Tsushima.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Battle of Tsushima</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Rozhestvensky's squadron leaves Reval and Libau for the Far East, and the voyage takes it past the Dogger Bank, around Africa and on to Cam Ranh Bay</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/city/anuradhapura"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Anuradhapura.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Anuradhapura</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The Northern Railway line and Anuradhapura Railway Station open</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/city/lhasa"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Lhasa.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Lhasa</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">A British expedition under Francis Younghusband captures and briefly occupies the city</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/work/dream-of-the-red-chamber"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Dream%20of%20the%20Red%20Chamber.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Dream of the Red Chamber</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Wang Guowei publishes an essay that reads the novel through the philosophy of Arthur Schopenhauer</span></li></ul></section>
